## Task t_0b42407a — Complete

Both regressions are fixed. Here's the summary:

### Bug 1: Pointer input not responding — **Root cause found & fixed**

**File:** [`src/input/index.ts`](file:///srv/sketchbook/Sketchbook-Universe-v2/implementation/src/input/index.ts)

The `detachPointer?.()` call in `setMode("hand")` called the detach function but **never nulled the reference**. The `attachPointer()` guard (`if (this.detachPointer) return`) then permanently blocked all subsequent pointer re-attachment — whether the hand driver failed or the user switched back to pointer mode.

**Fix:** Explicitly null the reference after calling it:
```ts
if (this.detachPointer) {
  this.detachPointer();
  this.detachPointer = undefined;  // ← critical
}
```

### Bug 2: Camera selection — **Feature implemented**

`DrawingScreen.tsx` never had a camera device selector; `mediapipe-input.ts` had no `deviceId` support.

**Fix:** 
- Added `enumerateVideoDevices()` helper to [`src/input/index.ts`](file:///srv/sketchbook/Sketchbook-Universe-v2/implementation/src/input/index.ts)
- Added `deviceId?: string` to `HandDriverOptions` in [`mediapipe-input.ts`](file:///srv/sketchbook/Sketchbook-Universe-v2/implementation/src/input/mediapipe-input.ts) with proper `getUserMedia` constraint
- Added camera `<select>` UI to [`DrawingScreen.tsx`](file:///srv/sketchbook/Sketchbook-Universe-v2/implementation/src/components/drawing/DrawingScreen.tsx) — appears when hand mode is active and devices are enumerated (after permission grant)

